A flex container measured for its max-content size (GetMaxContentSize, an indefinite inline size) builds its
items as grid items are built: cyclic inline percentages behave as auto, zero or none (CSS Sizing 3 5.2.1)
instead of resolving against the 10000 px stand-in, so a shrink-to-fit panel with a width: 100% child takes
its content's width. LayoutDetails::BuildIntrinsicHorizontalSize owns that rule for item boxes and item sizing.
The aspect-ratio refusal that IntrinsicWidth carried for grid items moves to the grid item checks, beside the
other grid refusals.

